# Source: HoareLogic.pdf, section "Exercises", "Single assignments", item 1.
id: assign-double
title: Doubling a variable
topic: Assignment
level: 1
source: HoareLogic.pdf, Exercises, "Single assignments" 1
tags: assignment, wp, consequence

task:
  Calculate the weakest precondition of the assignment for the
  postcondition $Q$. Then use the consequence rule to decide whether the
  triple is valid.

pre: x > 5
post: x > 10

program:
  {P}
  {R1}
  x := x * 2      // i1
  {Q}

verdict: valid

step: R1, the weakest precondition of x := x * 2
rule: ASSIGN, WP
focus: i1
text:
  The precondition of an assignment is obtained by substituting the
  assigned variable ($x$) with the assignment expression ($x * 2$) in the
  postcondition $Q$.
calc:
  wp(x := x * 2, Q)
  = (x > 10)[x <- x * 2]
  = x * 2 > 10            // x is replaced by x * 2
  = x > 5                 // divide both sides by 2
set: R1 = x > 5

step: P implies R1
rule: CONSEQUENCE
focus: P, R1
text:
  $R1$ is the weakest precondition of the program for $Q$. By the
  consequence rule, the triple is valid when the precondition $P$ implies
  $R1$.
  >>> «P» ==> «R1»
vc: x > 5 ==> x > 5
why:
  $P$ and $R1$ are the same formula, and every formula implies itself.
result: The triple is valid.
